= Occupation of Fiume

Gabriele D'Annunzio, a poet and officer of the Regio Esercito, along with his "legionaries", have seized control of the city of Fiume from Entente occupying forces, declaring the "Italian Regency of Carnaro" and demanding Italy annex the city.

D'Annunzio, accompanied by syndicalist Alceste De Ambris, has surprisingly garnered the support of some of the left, most notably the national syndicalist *Italian Labour Union*, and even more surprisingly, Vladimir Lenin, the leader of the current revolution in Russia.

British and French union organisations, however, have called upon Italian workers to protest this perceived act of imperialism, even though some of the them consider D'Annunzio to be righteous in his cause.

Regardless, this has caused quite a stir internationally, and will certainly delay the resolution of our negotiations with Yugoslavia.


